\title{AT-FD-7 · Actual augmented shapes and their diagram model}
\taxon{Acceptance test}
\meta{id}{AT-FD-7}
\meta{area}{foundation feasibility}
\meta{origin}{design/11-foundation-feasibility.md}
\meta{status}{proposed}
\meta{statement-version}{1}
\tag{acceptance-test}
\tag{area:fd}
\tag{status:proposed}

\p{Define the exact generating incidence data, operations, and equations of the set-level augmented VDC. Build the free/arity presentation with the hypotheses actually used by its nerve theorem. Validate \code{c₁^∅}, \code{(0,0)} cells and both their compositions, nullary inputs, mixed rows, and shared sides. Prove the no-horizontal fragment recovers 2-categories, including composition laws. Reject the attempted ordinary active \code{[0] → [1]} encoding of a one-input/empty-output transition. Supply the diagram model required by \code{MapRel} and \code{Mod}: Reedy/elegance if that route works, or a concrete alternative with the necessary cofibrant-source, relative restriction, and replacement results. A fallback is accepted only with those results. Prove any canonical encoding used by the prototype; flags or drawings alone are not an arity or normalization theorem.}
\p{\strong{Depends on:} minimal category/arity theory from the inventory. This gate supplies the shape prerequisites for \ref{at-fd-0003} and \ref{at-fd-0008}; it is not allowed to rely on them for the definition of its own category. \strong{Evidence:} algebra, shape presentation, nerve hypotheses, fragment comparison, and actual model lemmas. \strong{Failure response:} revise the presentation; if no workable augmented shape/model route exists, stop the current root track and produce a model-change decision.}
\p{Named by: \ref{dec-ch-0018}, \ref{dec-kr-0015}, \ref{dec-kr-0016}, \ref{dec-kr-0017}, \ref{dec-kr-0018}, \ref{dec-rt-0016}, \ref{dec-rt-0030}, \ref{dec-tl-0021}.}
\p{\strong{Partial implementation evidence:} \code{Kernel/Augmented/} implements incident generating cells, shared-side rows, concatenation laws, primitive operation types and both derived vertical-cell compositions. \code{Simplex.no_active_zero_to_one} and \code{Simplex.no_active_encoding} prove the ordinary-active obstruction. \code{FromTwoCategory.cellEquiv} and its identity, associativity and interchange laws verify the binary cell model of a supplied strict 2-category; \code{FromCat.cellNatTransEquiv} identifies the supplied Cat model with natural transformations and preserves both binary compositions. Concrete examples cover mixed rows, nullary input, nonidentity outside sides and the rejected intermediate-arrow mismatch. Names here are under \code{Kernel.Augmented}.}
\p{\strong{Algebra evidence:} \ref{augmented-algebra} records all five equation families in \code{Kernel.Augmented.Laws}, their explicit incident domains and the complete-boundary equality proofs. \code{Kernel.Augmented.AdditiveModel.algebra} proves them for arbitrary additive commutative cell labels over any supplied vertical category and horizontal graph. Mixed nested examples retain distinct cells; invalid intermediate factorizations and empty inner rows are rejected. The equation fields are obligations on arbitrary operation data, with a checked nontrivial model, rather than unconditional claims about all operations.}
\p{\strong{Transport and extraction evidence:} \ref{augmented-transport} separates row shapes from cell labels with checked round trips. Substitution boundaries compute from shapes, and algebra equations use ordinary equality after explicit complete-boundary transport. \code{Vertical.bicategory} and \code{Vertical.bicategory_strict} extract Mathlib's strict 2-category from an algebra, deriving both compositions and coherence. \ref{augmented-comparison} now proves the reverse \code{FromTwoCategory.algebra}, comparison round trips, arbitrary incident substitution compatibility and discrete hom-nerve isomorphisms.}
\p{\strong{Still open:} the actual arity presentation and its unconditional augmented nerve recognition theorem, any canonical encoding theorem, and all required labelled diagram-model results. This partial evidence does not pass or weaken the current gate; status remains proposed and statement-version remains 1.}
\p{\em{Reproduction:} \code{docs/augmented/README.md} pins Definition 1.2 and Example 1.5 of Koudenburg arXiv:1910.11189v4 and lists checked declarations and remaining obligations. \code{lake build Augmented} and \code{python3 scripts/check_foundations.py} compile and transitively audit the entire new namespace against the approved axioms; \code{docs/foundations/inventory.json} records exact types, source hashes, dependencies and axiom closures.}

\p{\strong{Relative free-cell evidence:} \ref{augmented-free-cells} proves the generated-congruence quotient laws and universal mapping property over a fixed vertical category and horizontal graph, with finite raw-term support. \ref{augmented-generating} extends this to an explicit generating presheaf base, free vertical paths and a global free mapping property. \ref{augmented-global-adjunction} adds the checked global free/forgetful adjunction and induced monad. Monadicity is now proved in \ref{augmented-monadicity}; the arity density and exactness hypotheses remain open.}

\p{\strong{Monad-algebra reconstruction evidence:} \ref{augmented-monad-vertical} reconstructs vertical categories and functors from arbitrary generating-monad algebras, retains the horizontal graph and proves a natural equivalence recovering each existing augmented algebra's vertical category. \ref{augmented-monad-cells} adds incident cells, all primitive operations and a surjective full-boundary evaluation map preserving both identities and arbitrary substitution. \ref{augmented-monadicity} now proves all five reconstructed equation families, identifies the action and proves essential surjectivity and monadicity. \ref{augmented-arity-nerve} constructs the actual nerve square and its canonical comparison, proving conditional recognition under density and comparison invertibility. \ref{augmented-finite-incidence} supplies a small dense candidate family; its monad exactness and the labelled diagram model remain open.}

\p{\strong{Finite incidence candidate:} \ref{augmented-finite-incidence} proves closure of finite generators under complete incidence, filtered reconstruction of each generating presheaf, and the equivalence between finite incidence and finite presentability. It constructs a small fully faithful dense candidate family of finite incidence diagrams and applies the conditional nerve theorem. Canonical-comparison invertibility for the generating monad remains open; no normalization or labelled diagram-model result is asserted. The full acceptance statements and statuses remain unchanged.}

\p{\strong{Finitary exactness reduction:} \code{GeneratingFiniteNerve} proves filtered-colimit preservation by the finite-incidence base nerve, factorization through finite supports, and finite-stage witnesses for equality of maps. \code{freeNerveComparison_eq} identifies the actual comparison on each arity of a fully faithful family with the representable Kan-extension isomorphism. \code{isIso_of_finiteIncidence} detects isomorphisms of filtered-colimit-preserving functors on the small finite family. Consequently, \code{finiteIncidence_exactness_iff_finitary} proves global canonical-comparison invertibility equivalent to filtered-colimit preservation by the actual generating monad. The augmented nerve theorem follows under this one remaining hypothesis; finitarity itself and the labelled diagram model remain open. Acceptance statements, versions and statuses are unchanged.}
